B.acs=new A.ex("Differential: a naive-Bayes model. Each category starts from a prior set by the clinical setting (equal priors by default) and every finding adds a log-likelihood weight; a softmax turns the totals into probabilities.",!1,null)
B.acw=new A.ex("Weights are the editor's conservative reading of published sensitivity, specificity and likelihood ratios (for example pooled LR+ \u2248 5 for ictal eye closure; lateral tongue bite specificity \u2248 100% vs PNES; urinary incontinence LR+ \u2248 0.9). Each carries a grade: A meta-analysis, systematic review or validated score; B cohort or video-EEG series; C expert teaching.",!1,null)
B.acv=new A.ex("Probabilities are tempered and mixed with 5% of a uniform distribution, so the app never shows more than about 96%: certainty would be false precision for an unvalidated model.",!1,null)
B.acx=new A.ex("Correlated findings are damped: within a group (automatisms, convulsive signs, presyncope, PNES motor signs) only the strongest counts in full and the rest at half.",!1,null)
B.acC=new A.ex("Calgary Syncope\u2013Seizure Score is computed exactly as published (Sheldon 2002) and shown separately: it is validated for seizure vs syncope, not PNES.",!1,null)
B.act=new A.ex("Cardiac and neurological red flags (ESC 2018 high-risk features and others) are never averaged into the estimate; they are shown first.",!1,null)
B.acA=new A.ex("Lateralization uses approximate positive predictive values of lateralizing signs (Loddenkemper & Kotagal 2005), assuming left-hemisphere dominance.",!1,null)
B.acu=new A.ex("Localization weights and some category weights (grade C) remain teaching-based.",!0,null)
